    validate --stability N: reject tasks whose tests flip between runs
    
    A task was validated by one failing run and one passing run. A test
    that passes 70% of the time passes that check and then fails agents at
    random forever, and in a benchmark that prints p-values a flaky task is
    noise dressed as signal.
    
    --stability 3 re-runs the fixed state and rejects any task where a test's
    outcome moved, naming the test. Default stays 1, so nothing changes for
    existing task sets; the manifest records the setting so a citation
    carries it. The fixture for the test is deterministically flaky (fails
    on exactly the third run in a tree), so the test of the flakiness
    detector is not itself flaky.
    
    Closes #32
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

